\subsection{Epistemic Closure}
Epistemic closure is achieved when:

\begin{enumerate}
    \item all invariants remain locked,
    \item all conservation laws propagate cleanly,
    \item all solvers remain bounded,
    \item all hardware substrates reproduce identical results.
\end{enumerate}

Under these conditions, tactile accessibility becomes irrelevant. Proof is
established through invariance, not touch.

This epistemological foundation forms the backbone of the unified system and
governs all subsequent sections of this journal.